        "original_id": "eb5d7dca-0531-5efe-9aba-13a4aa7b3a91",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Events: Symphony Splash\n- People: Tania Miller, Pyotr Ilyich Tchaikovsky, Napoleon\n- Organizations: Victoria Symphony\n- Works: 1812 Overture\n- Concepts: Russia's defence against the Grande Armée in 1812\n\nFacts:\n- In 1812, Russia defended its motherland against Napoleon's invading Grande Armée.\n- In 1880, Pyotr Ilyich Tchaikovsky wrote The Year 1812, a festival overture in E-flat major, Op. 49, popularly known as the 1812 Overture, to commemorate Russia's defence in 1812.\n- Tania Miller is the Music Director of the Victoria Symphony.\n- The concert Symphony Splash is led by Victoria Symphony Music Director Tania Miller.",
